1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,000
RideScore DC — running on one laptop, from public data

2
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:11,500
Every street coloured by how comfortable it is to cycle on

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Underneath: census blocks scored by PeopleForBikes' BNA —
what each block can reach without high-stress streets

4
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:24,500
Two models. Two geometries. Two producers. One map.

5
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:30,000
Hover: what is this?

6
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:35,000
Click: everything about it

7
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:41,000
One click, one answer — the street, then the block beneath it

8
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:48,500
Every label and unit comes from the pipeline.
Nothing here was typed into the website.

9
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:56,000
RideScore and traffic stress: two layers, one road network

10
00:00:56,500 --> 00:01:03,000
Geometry fetched once — and one at a time,
because both colour the same lines

11
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:10,000
This file is what the website was told

12
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:15,500
Geographies — what is scored, and how one is identified

13
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Sources — where the geometry comes from

14
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:24,500
Layers — one value, drawn one way

15
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:30,000
A colour scale, a domain, fields with labels and units

16
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:35,500
Half of it: the presentation — what this deployment publishes

17
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:41,500
Half of it: the dataset descriptions, written beside the code
that produces each dataset

18
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:48,000
This is everything the frontend knows about the data

19
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:54,000
Three ways to draw. Two ways to deliver. One kind of scale.

20
00:01:54,500 --> 00:02:00,000
No "RideScore". No "BNA". No table or column names.

21
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:05,500
Read the manifest, add each source once, draw each layer

22
00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:11,000
BNA publishes more scores than this map draws

23
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:16,000
Ten lines of presentation: recreation

24
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:21,000
Regenerate the manifest — 0.8 seconds

25
00:02:21,500 --> 00:02:27,000
Title, legend, popup, and a 0–1 scale
taken from the attribute's description

26
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:33,000
No frontend change. No rebuild. No deploy.

27
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:39,000
Now publish something this page cannot draw

28
00:02:39,500 --> 00:02:45,000
Dropped — and everything else still draws

29
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:50,000
So the pipeline and the website can be released separately

30
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:56,000
Descriptions are checked against the data

31
00:02:56,500 --> 00:03:03,000
The first run found three places where the pipeline
was not producing what it claimed

32
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:09,000
Not here yet: the weight sliders, and the query endpoint

33
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:14,500
Neither needs the frontend to change

34
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:20,000
All of it: one laptop, a 3 MB download
